### Tests for the Identity and Administration API (Daniel)
### Click "Send Request" above each test. The comment says what should come back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3003
# Cloudflare's test ticket. With the test secret key it always passes.
@ticket = XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX

# Copy these two from the T12 answer (the entry with daniel.test.student@example.com):
# requestId = the "id" of that entry,  studentId = the "id" inside its "user"
@requestId = 8ccb9e27-605a-4711-a394-590b15ae1c4d
@studentId = 91e47e82-ed87-4e12-b7d8-83ac4f3f91c8

# Badges are filled in automatically from the login answers (T10 and T15).
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}
@adminId = {{adminLogin.response.body.user.id}}
@studentToken = {{studentLogin.response.body.token}}


############################## SIGN UP AND LOGIN ##############################

### T1. Health check  -> 200 "status": "ok"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### T2. Sign up WITHOUT a Turnstile ticket  -> 403 BOT_CHECK_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test Student", "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123", "role": "student" }

### T3. Sign up a student (correct)  -> 201, accountStatus "pending"  (already done, run only once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Test Student", "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123", "role": "student" }

### T4. Same email again  -> 409 EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Copy Cat", "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123", "role": "student" }

### T5. Try to sign up as admin  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Sneaky", "email": "daniel.test.sneaky@example.com", "password": "Sneaky123", "role": "admin" }

### T6. Weak password  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Weak", "email": "daniel.test.weak@example.com", "password": "123", "role": "student" }

### T7. Log in while still pending  -> 403 ACCOUNT_PENDING  (only before T13 approves her)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123" }

### T8. Log in with the WRONG password  -> 401 "Email or password is incorrect."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Wrong12345" }

### T9. Log in with an email that doesn't exist  -> 401, SAME message as T8
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "Whatever123" }

### T10. Log in as the admin  -> 200 with a "token"
### The email and password come from admin-api/.env (ADMIN_TEST_EMAIL, ADMIN_TEST_PASSWORD),
### so no admin password is ever written in this file or in GitHub.
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_TEST_EMAIL}}", "password": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_TEST_PASSWORD}}" }


############################## ADMIN POWERS ##############################

### T11. Admin area with NO badge  -> 401 AUTH_REQUIRED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications

### T12. Admin: the waiting list  -> 200, find daniel.test.student@example.com and copy the two ids
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T13. Admin approves the student  -> 200 "Account approved", accountStatus "active"  (already done)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "approved" }

### T14. Decide the SAME request again  -> 409 VERIFICATION_ALREADY_REVIEWED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "rejected" }

### T15. The student can log in  -> 200 with a "token"
# @name studentLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123" }

### T16. Student tries the admin area with their own badge  -> 403 FORBIDDEN
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### T17. Admin suspends the student  -> 200 "Account suspended."
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{studentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "suspended" }

### T18. Suspend her again  -> 409 INVALID_STATUS_CHANGE
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{studentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "suspended" }

### T19. Suspended student tries to log in  -> 403 ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123" }

### T20. Admin tries to suspend THEMSELVES  -> 403 CANNOT_CHANGE_ADMIN
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{adminId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "suspended" }

### T21. Admin reactivates the student  -> 200 "Account reactivated."
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{studentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "active" }

### T22. Wrong decision word  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "maybe" }

### T23. Request id that doesn't exist  -> 404 VERIFICATION_NOT_FOUND
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/verifications/11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "approved" }


############################## AUDIT LOG ##############################

### T24. Diary: only suspensions from the admin desk  -> 200, shows the T17 suspension
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/logs?service=admin&action=SUSPEND_USER
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T25. Diary: logins today (change the date if needed)  -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/logs?action=LOGIN&from=2026-11-22&to=2026-11-22
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### T26. Diary with a parameter we don't allow  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/logs?sort=newest
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}